.DS_Store
node_modules
/build
/.svelte-kit
/package
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
vite.config.js.timestamp-*
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# Isolated agent worktrees are materialised inside the repo. Each one is a
# full checkout, so without this a `git add -A` from any tool or agent would
# try to commit an entire second copy of the tree into the tree.
.claude/worktrees/

# Internal strategy notes — kept locally, not published. See README.
docs/positioning.md

# The driven UI test writes its row report here on every run — evidence for the
# run you just did, not something to keep.
e2e/last-run.json
/target

# The XCFramework is a build product — 432MB of compiled Rust for two
# architectures, rebuilt by `scripts/build-xcframework.sh` whenever the FFI
# surface changes. The *generated Swift* beside it (apple/Generated) is
# deliberately NOT ignored: it is small, it is the boundary's actual shape,
# and having it in review is how a moved API becomes visible rather than a
# link error later.
/apple/Supermessage.xcframework/

# Brainstorming companion scratch
.superpowers/

# Xcode
apple/Supermessage.xcodeproj/

# The Android `.so` files are the same build product as the XCFramework above,
# and ignored for the same reason plus a harder one: 362MB across four ABIs,
# with the x86 slice alone over GitHub's 100MB per-file limit. Rebuilt by
# `scripts/build-android-libs.sh`. The *generated Kotlin* beside them
# (android/core/src/main/kotlin) is deliberately NOT ignored, exactly as the
# generated Swift is not.
android/core/src/main/jniLibs/
